<title>UK: Corn ship leaves collision site for Taiwan.</title>
<headline>Corn ship leaves collision site for Taiwan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Singapore-flag bulk carrier Neptune Aldebaran, which was involved in a collision off western Japan on Tuesday, departed the site the following evening for Taiwan, Lloyd's Shipping Intelligence Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 66,764 dwt ship had been sailing from the United States for Taiwan laden with corn when it was in collision with the South Korean-registered Dongjin Hope.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders said on Wednesday the accident would delay the bulk carrier's Taiwan-bound cargo of 54,000 tonnes of corn and temporarily boost local corn prices.</p>
<p>The 1,975 dwt Dongjin Hope left the site in the tow of a tug on Wednesday evening and arrived safely in Busan, South Korea, on Thursday morning.</p>
</text>
